WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:15.220
Choose the Investor workspace. Start with the role that matches your task. The platform explains the journey before you request access.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:26.520
Use the demonstration profile. Request fictional preview access, then open the workspace. No live identity provider is connected.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:37.820
Begin with the next action. The dashboard prioritises one useful next step and keeps role-specific navigation easy to find.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:49.120
Find an available opportunity. Status labels distinguish the reviewable reference case from opportunities that are still in diligence.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:01:00.420
Understand the asset and structure. Review the equipment, project vehicle, SME relationship and the rights represented by each digital unit.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:11.720
Read the risks before scenarios. Operating, asset, liquidity and structural risks appear before illustrative cash-flow outcomes.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:23.020
Check the evidence status. Each document is marked recorded, draft or conditional so incomplete evidence stays visible.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:34.320
Complete the comprehension step. Choose an illustrative amount and confirm the rights, liquidity limits and cash-flow dependency.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:45.620
Create an attributable record. The demonstration receipt connects the amount, disclosure version and environment without moving money.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:56.920
Return to guidance at any time. The Learning Centre provides short role guides, plain-language definitions and observable next actions.
